---
---

<section id="video" class="sec" data-mascot-hide>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="hm-headline">
      <span class="hm-paper hm-label hm-label--display strip-lg hm-tilt-r1" data-reveal>55 SECONDS, CUT PAPER</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="video-grid">
      <div class="hm-frame">
        {/* The 8 MB clip is not in the HTML until asked for: no bytes are transferred while the
            visitor reads the text next to it. `preload="none"` + a poster keeps the box painted. */}
        <button type="button" class="video-play" data-video-load aria-label="Play the video, sound on">
          <img src="/assets/frame-title.jpg" alt="" width="1080" height="1350" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <span class="video-play__badge hm-paper hm-paper--yellow hm-tilt-r1">▶ PLAY — SOUND ON</span>
        </button>
        <video
          id="story-video"
          controls
          muted
          playsinline
          preload="none"
          poster="/assets/frame-title.jpg"
          width="1080"
          height="1350"
          hidden
        >
          <source data-src="/assets/hamdi-ai-reboot.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          Your browser can't play this video. The transcript below tells the same story.
        </video>
      </div>

      <div class="video-side">
        <p class="narrator narrator--lg">The story above, in stop-motion. Sound on.</p>
        <button type="button" class="hm-button hm-button--ghost" data-play-sound>Play with sound</button>
        <details class="transcript">
          <summary>Read the transcript</summary>
          <p class="hm-paper card hm-tilt-r1">
            Once upon a time, there was Hamdi. Sixteen years of code… and one plot twist. For twelve years, he was Tech Lead at
            Prisma Media, keeping Gala and Harper's Bazaar fast for millions of readers. No pressure. Then the media world
            started changing fast. Hamdi spotted a new path… and took it. So he did the bravest thing a developer can do. He
            switched caps. Now he's back in school: the MSc AIMS, AI for Marketing Strategy, at EPITA and EM Normandie. He
            talks to language models all day. They talk back. What does he bring? Sixteen years of production code, a nose for
            scale, latency and cost, and GenAI tools developers actually install. And now, he's looking for a six-month
            internship as an Applied or Forward Deployed AI Engineer. Scan the code. Say hi. He's friendly.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
